<title>HONG KONG: First Tractor debuts at HK$6.00/share.</title>
<headline>First Tractor debuts at HK$6.00/share.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Chinese agricultural tractor maker First Tractor Co Ltd made their trading debut at HK$6.00 per share on Monday, compared with an issue price of HK$4.50.  </p>
<p>First Tractor issued 300 million H-shares at HK$4.50 each in a global offering -- 255 million shares placed with international investors and 45 million shares offered to the Hong Kong public.</p>
<p>The Hong Kong public offering was 296.4 times subscribed.</p>
<p>The company said it would use the proceeds to finance expansion of its manufacturing capacity, repay debt and for working capital.</p>
<p>H-shares are shares of Chinese incorporated companies listed in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6370.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
